-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",417,{
[13313]="70067C49\n1\tSpeak with the stable-master and ride to Rakhatâb\tKhôltekh's emissary directed you to the stable-master in Jax Phanâl to purchase a ride south along the road to Rakhatâb.\n2\tSpeak with Nûrut\tYou should take a stabled horse to the southern fortress of Rakhatâb. There you are to meet with the foreman, Nûrut. He has been told of your arrival and all the deeds you have done to assist the citizens of Jax Phanâl.\n",
[13314]="700266DF\n1\tAid Maladan with Gateways to the Past\030Aid Nethrandir with Plunderers of History\030Aid Rodlam with Foulness from the Deep\030Aid Maladan with Keys to the Crypts\030Aid Nimbellas with Eastern Gate to Annúminas\tThe Rangers at the camp within the Way of Kings need help scouting the surrounding area.\n2\tTalk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings\tNimbellas will be pleased to hear that the Way of Kings has been thoroughly scouted.\n",
[13315]="700455DB\n1\tTalk to Hutha in Taur Drúadan\tHutha can be found within the War-stead of the King's Men. Burnoth has asked you to speak with Hutha about his plan for crossing through the Enemy's blockade beneath Amon Dîn.\n2\tTravel to the summit of Amon Dîn\tAmon Dîn can be found far to the south-east of the War-stead of the King's Men. Hutha has asked you to travel to the summit of Amon Dîn and light the extinguished beacon.\n3\tLight the beacon of Amon Dîn\tA suitable torch can be found on the beacon at Amon Dîn. You have reached the summit of Amon Dîn and should now light the beacon to distract the Enemy's forces below.\n4\tMeet the Riders Three at the Field of Onslaught\tThe Riders Three can be found at the Field of Onslaught. You have cleared a passage to the Pelennor Fields for the Riders Three and should now journey to their side. Note: You must complete Book 5, Chapter 8 of Volume IV to advance this objective.\n5\tTalk to Burnoth at the Field of Onslaught\tBurnoth can be found somewhere on the Pelennor Fields. You have arrived at the Pelennor Fields and should now seek out the Riders Three.\n",
[13316]="7004E6C1\n1\tScout the path to Glimmerdeep\tYou should scout ahead of the expedition, west from Skarháld, along the path up Thrumfall Mountain, where Glimmerdeep can be found.\n2\tEavesdrop on a Gundabad Guard\030Defeat Gundabad guards (total: 2)\tYou should eavesdrop on and defeat the Orcs guarding the path to Glimmerdeep.\n3\tTalk to Hórin on the path\tYou should talk to Hórin on the path to Glimmerdeep.\n",
[13317]="7006689B\n1\tFind Egnir in Alagrant\tEgnir can likely be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. Uidor has asked you to find Egnir, one of Lord Duinhir's most skilled bowmen, after he took an unexpected leave of his duties in Morlad.\n2\tTalk to Calennen\tCalennen can be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. Having found no sign of Egnir, you should talk to the hunters of Alagrant and learn if he passed through the hamlet on some errand. You should talk to Calennen.\n3\tTalk to Sarnir\tSarnir can be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. Calennen recalls that Egnir visited Alagrant, but left after a short time. He thinks Sarnir might know more about Egnir's whereabouts. You should talk to Sarnir.\n4\tFind the carving on a tree outside Alagrant\tThe carving can be found on a tree to the south-west of Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. Sarnir spied Egnir making a carving into a tree outside Alagrant. You should find the carving and examine it.\n5\tExamine the defaced carving\tThe defaced carving can be found on a tree to the south-west of Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. You have spotted the carving on a nearby tree outside Alagrant, but it has been defaced. You should examine it.\n6\tTalk to Sarnir\tSarnir can be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. You have found a carving reading 'E+D', but it is unclear why Egnir defaced it. You should return to Sarnir.\n",
[13318]="7000EABB\n1\tFind the wayward bull\tThe wayward bull may be nearby, among the mountains north of Sûri-kylä and Ilmo's camp. Ilmo fears that his prize bull has been taken by the peikko and has asked you to search for him.\n2\tTalk to Ilmo\tIlmo is outside of Sûri-kylä, north from its gates. You should return to Ilmo and let him know that his bull has been returned safely.\n",
[13319]="7006138B\n1\tThe other children might know where Periwinkle has gone. They're all playing near the Elbow's Bend Inn.\t\n2\tTalk to Gildor at Tighfield's western gate\tGildor is waiting for you by Tighfield's western gate. You should discuss what you've discovered with him.\n3\tMeet up with Gildor outside Tham Amothir\tGildor has suggested regrouping outside the ruins of Tham Amothir, to the south-west of Tighfield.\n4\tTalk to Gildor\tYou've found Gildor outside Tham Amothir. You should talk to him to decide on what to do next.\n",
[13320]="70008282\n1\tSearch for Lagorlam in Taur Gonwaith\tLagorlam has gone to the forest of Taur Gonwaith, south-east of Lin Giliath. Thaliollang has sent you to find Lagorlam and make certain he is well.\n",
[13321]="70061F08\n1\tSearch for the missing Mayor\tRhiangar Nevit has asked you locate her father, Mayor Cadwallon Nevit, in Tharbad. Tharbad is located in south-west Cardolan.\n2\tTalk to the Mayor\tYou have discovered the missing Mayor, but he seems to have been knocked down. You should talk to the Mayor. The Mayor is in Tharbad, in south-east Cardolan.\n3\tCollect the Mayor's staff\tMayor Cadwallon Nevit has asked you to bring him back his thrown staff. The staff is on the road near the Mayor, in Tharbad.\n4\tGive the Mayor his staff\tYou have rescued the wayward Mayor, Cadwallon Nevit. You should talk to the Mayor and let him know his daughter is waiting for him. Mayor Nevit is in Tharbad, in south-east Cardolan.\n",
[13322]="7006989D\n1\tTalk to Khâhir the Quick outside the arena\tMokhlêsh asked you to collect his winnings from Khâhir the Quick outside the arena.\n2\tThe upstart who stole the wager can be found outside the Raven and Albatross in the Upper Ward.\t\n3\tReturn the wayward wager to Khâhir the Quick outside the arena\tKhâhir the Quick is outside the arena.\n4\tBring the wager to Mokhlêsh at the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward\tMokhlêsh is at the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward.\n",
[13323]="7005934F\n1\tScout Blomley Sward\030Scout Helva's Edge\030Scout Hunter's Ledge\030Scout the East-delf\030Scout the West-delf\030Collect ore samples (total: 8)\030Collect pelts from beasts in the Wildwood (total: 8)\tBlomley Sward, Helva's Edge, Hunter's Ledge, the East-delf, and the West-delf can all be found in the Wildwood. You should collect ore samples and animal pelts from moose, wolves, bears, and boars, for the League of the Axe as you survey the Wildwood.\n2\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting\tEnid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.\n3\tRepair broken bear traps (total: 5)\030Repair broken fish traps (total: 5)\030Sharpen dull pickaxes (total: 5)\tBroken traps and dull pickaxes can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should repair these items for the League of the Axe.\n4\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting\tEnid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.\n",
[13324]="7004D08B\n1\tTell Bryn a Story of your adventures\tBryn can be found in the Great-keep in Dale. You should tell Prince Bryn stories of your adventures.\n2\tLook for a guard on the southern bridge\tBryn fled to the south in Dale. Look for a guard on the southern bridge of Dale to see if he has stopped Bryn.\n3\tTalk to the southern bridge guard in Dale\tTalk to the guard on the southern bridge out of Dale and find out if he has seen Bryn.\n4\tTalk to the southern bridge guard in Dale\tTalk to the guard on the southern bridge out of Dale.\n5\tTalk to King Bard II\030Talk to Prince Bryn\tYou should speak with both King Bard II and Prince Bryn, who can be found in the Great-keep in Dale.\n6\tTalk to Erna\tYou should speak with Queen Regent Erna, who can be found in the Great-keep in Dale.\n",
[13325]="7003EA7F\n1\tFree Dunlendings from Isengard debris (total: 8)\tDunlendings can be found near the ruined ring of Isengard in Nan Curunír. You have discovered Dunlendings trapped by rubble in the aftermath of the Battle of Isengard. You should free them and send them on their way.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have freed many Dunlendings from the ruins of Isengard.\n",
[13326]="7006C6E2\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai captors at Ar-jirush ([see journal]/10)\030Rescue the captured merchant from Ar-jirush\tRaphûz asked for your help in gaining an audience with Ashâmi's father. He believes that rescuing his other daughter's husband from Ordâkhai captivity could be the boon he needs to gain an audience with Ashâmi's father.\n2\tReturn to Jirush and speak with Raphûz\tYou succeeded in rescuing Ardub and culled many of the Ordâkhai from Ar-jirush. Return to Raphûz with the news.\n3\tSpeak with the merchant Igbâl at Jirush\tMake your way across Jirush to Igbâl. Tell the man you rescued his daughter's husband.\n4\tSpeak with Igbâl's translator, Galamê\tIgbâl would not speak with you, but his translator drew your attention. You should speak with him.\n5\tTalk to Raphûz\tGalamê, Igbâl's translator, asked you to inform Raphûz that they want to meet him at his earliest convenience. Return to Raphûz, at his location in Jirush, and share the news.\n",
[13327]="7004CE97\n1\tTalk to folk in Dale about the Easterling refugees.\t\n2\tHear what's going on in Dale\tReturn to Dale.\n3\tFind the cause of the shouting\tYou should go to the location where you heard shouting, in the lower markets, in the south-eastern quarter of Dale.\n4\tThe Dale-men have encircled the unarmed Easterling man in the lower markets, in the south-east of Dale. You should persuade the Dale-men to leave the Easterling man alone.\t\n5\tTalk to the Easterling Man\tYou should talk to the Easterling refugee, whom you rescued in the south-eastern quarter of Dale.\n6\tReturn to King Bard II\tYou should return to King Bard II, who can be found in the Great-keep in the north of Dale, and bring word of all you saw and heard among the Dale-folk.\n",
[13328]="7004E907\n1\tPolish road markers (total: 20)\tYou should polish road markers that can be found along the path between Erebor and Dôm Goru in Ered Mithrin.\n2\tTalk to Rúzat at Dôm Goru\tYou should talk to Rúzat, who can be found at Dôm Goru in Ered Mithrin.\n",
[13329]="7006823F\n1\tTalk to Elder Roshat\tTalk to Elder Roshat in the Elder Hall.\n2\tInvestigate the southern cliffs near the Mâkhda Khorbo\tElder Roshat has asked you to go to the hills east of Khûtra, to the cliffs facing south near the ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo and investigate the source of the disease.\n3\tPatch the stones seeping noxious blight ([see journal]/3)\tA noxious blight is seeping from these broken stones. Patch up the stones and seal the wellspring!\n4\tTalk to Heshra, the herbalist\tTalk to Heshra, the herbalist in the Elder Hall.\n",
[13330]="7002E559\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Harsterre\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13331]="7002E586\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Warin\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13332]="7002E558\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Fréamar\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13333]="7002E592\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Oseg\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13334]="7002EF55\n1\tDefeat Orcs at the Sutcrofts barricade (total: 5)\030Defeat an Orc-leader at the Sutcrofts barricade (quantity: see journal)\tThe pass to the Sutcrofts is located south-west of Parth Galen and has been barricaded by the Orcs. You need to defeat the Orcs to allow Hestil's company to pass.\n2\tCúfaron is waiting to speak with you. You have defeated Orcs at the barricade into the Sutcrofts and should return to tell Cúfaron.\t\n",
[13335]="70036A32\n1\tSearch the road in the Westfold for signs of Théoden's company\tKing Théoden, along with Éomer, Aragorn, Legolas, and Gimli, have begun a journey towards the Fords of Isen. You should meet the king and his company upon the east-to-west road in the Westfold to lend them aid at the brink of war.\n2\tSpeak with someone in the small company on the road\tYou have spotted a gathering of people on the road in the centre of the Westfold. You should speak with someone in this company to get word of Gandalf or King Théoden.\n3\tAsk the refugees if they need any assistance\tYou have spotted a gathering of people on the road in the centre of the Westfold. You should ask the refugees if they need assistance.\n4\tSearch for Théoden at Helm's Dike\tHelm's Deep is in the valley in the south-western corner of the Westfold. You should ride with all speed to the gate of the stronghold of Helm's Deep.\n",
[13336]="700374CB\n1\tFollow the trail of felled trees leading north-west\tFelled trees can be found north-west of Marton. You should follow the trail of felled trees to discover what has been destroying them.\n2\tFollow the trail of felled trees leading north-west (total: 8)\tFelled trees can be found north-west of Marton. You should follow the trail of felled trees to discover what has been destroying them.\n3\tDiscover the source of the felled trees\tThe source of the felled trees can be found north-west of Marton. You should discover the source of the felled trees.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have discovered a large encampment of trolls, too close to Marton for your comfort. This path is certainly not safe for the refugees.\n",
[13337]="7003A474\n1\tDefeat enemies in Madh-fushaum (0/24)\tThe army gathered within Madh-fushaum is mostly comprised of ragtag Dunlendings, but they are mingled with Orcs and Uruk-hai. You should defeat as many as possible.\n2\tDefeat enemies in Madh-fushaum (total: 20)\tThe army gathered within Madh-fushaum is mostly comprised of ragtag Dunlendings, but they are mingled with Orcs and Uruk-hai. You should defeat as many as possible.\n3\tComplete\tThere are far too many of the enemy gathered in Madh-fushaum for one to handle alone. However, those that remain will never forget the day the you stepped foot in Madh-fushaum.\n",
[13338]="70030CCE\n1\tThe emblems and marks of Saruman are plain to see on all of his fell servants. You should collect tokens of proof of the Wizard's betrayal while you rid the forest of his servants.\t\n2\tCollect proof of Saruman's folly (total: 8)\tSymbols of the White Hand are on the Orcs and Uruks at the pond near Oldheart's meadow. You should collect tokens of proof of the Wizard's betrayal while you rid the forest of his servants.\n3\tBring the evidence to Oldheart\tOldheart is in his meadow at the foot of a flower-spotted hill in Fangorn's western eaves. You should bring the proof of Saruman's wrongdoing to Oldheart.\n",
[13339]="700622DB\n1\tDefeat the invading Wargs (total: 6)\tThe site of the Warg attacks can be found to the north of Echad Terthas, across the river. Duindil has asked you to defeat any Wargs in the area.\n2\tCollect a Warg pelt as proof\tYou should probably get proof of your success.\n3\tTalk to Duindil\tYou were able to obtain a Warg's pelt. Duindil should find this useful in the investigation. Duindil can be found in Echad Terthas outside of Caras Gelebren. Return to Duindil.\n4\tDeliver the pelt to Rhovandis at Idhobel\tRhovandis can be found in Idhobel, located in Western Eregion and north-east of Echad Terthas. Duindil has asked you to deliver the Warg's pelt to Rhovandis.\n",
[13340]="7000B93E\n1\tCollect arrows from the carcass of the white hart\tWistan thinks the carcass must be somewhere to the west of Echad Candelleth, between the dwelling-places of the Gauredain and the Wood-trolls. Wistan has asked you to search for the carcass of the white hart, which he tracked across the Trollshaws, and return to Echad Candelleth with both it and the arrows with which he brought it down.\n",
[13341]="70034C38\n1\tSpeak to Hereswith\tHereswith is inside Edsig's house, near the stables and centre of Forlaw. Hereswith is trying to stay busy with household tasks, and not focus on the events of the day.\n2\tPick up Gárferth's shield\tGárferth's shield is kept in the bedroom of Edsig's home.\n3\tPlace Gárferth's shield at Edsig's grave\tThe path to the graveyard of Forlaw is just outside Forlaw's southern gate.\n4\tCompleted\tRespects have been paid to Edsig.\n",
[13342]="70034C3F\n1\tSpeak to Ebba\tEbba is inside Gárferth's house, near the centre of Forlaw. Ebba and Ansith are preparing dinner after the long day.\n2\tTake Edsig's helmet\tEdsig's helmet is kept on a shelf in the main room of Gárferth's home.\n3\tPlace Edsig's helmet at Gárferth's grave\tThe path to the graveyard of Forlaw is just outside Forlaw's southern gate.\n4\tCompleted\tRespects have been paid to Gárferth.\n",
[13343]="70034C3E\n1\tSpeak to Burghild\tBurghild is inside Gársig's house on the western side of Forlaw. Burghild is doing anything she can to keep herself from falling apart entirely, as she must keep it together for her only remaining son.\n2\tTake Gársig's sword\tGársig's sword is kept on the dresser in the sleeping quarters of Gársig's Home.\n3\tPlace Gársig's sword at his grave\tThe path to the graveyard of Forlaw is just outside Forlaw's southern gate.\n4\tCompleted\tRespects have been paid to Gársig.\n",
[13344]="700375C1\n1\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should bring Dudsig's recommendation to Reeve Fríthild's attention.\n2\tUse the camp-fire to summon Reeve Fríthild and her companions\tReeve Fríthild's encampment lies to the west of Stoke. Reeve Fríthild instructed you to meet her party at her encampment.\n3\tUse the camp-fire to summon Reeve Fríthild and her companions\tReeve Fríthild's encampment lies to the west of Stoke. Reeve Fríthild instructed you to meet her party at her encampment.\n4\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tReeve Fríthild is at her encampment, west of Stoke. You should speak with Reeve Fríthild regarding the recent battle.\n5\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild in Stoke\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke, east of her encampment. Reeve Fríthild has asked you to speak with her in Stoke.\n",
})
